{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>But we alone</b> — It is read with a vav and written with an alef (ולא), and he explained: 'and we do not sacrifice to any besides Him.'" "<b>It is not for you [to build] with us</b> — Its meaning: that you should intermingle with us to build the house of our Elohim."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The kethiv (ולא, 'and not') vs. qeri (ולא, 'to him alone') distinction turns on consonantal identity with different vocalization; Ibn Ezra cites the traditional explanation that the written form with alef yields the sense 'and we do not sacrifice to any besides Him.' The subject of 'he explained' is unclear — possibly a prior exegete.", 1 "The lemma לא לכם ולנו reflects the phrase in Ezra 4:3 rather than 4:2; the comment addresses the opponents' refusal wording."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:51.671440970Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}